_model: definition
---
title: Definition 22
---
order: 22
---
short_label: I.Def.22
---
statement: Of quadrilateral figures, a <i>square</i> is that which is both equilateral and right-angled; an <i>oblong</i> that which is right-angled but not equilateral; a <i>rhombus</i> that which is equilateral but not right-angled; and a <i>rhomboid</i> that which has its opposite sides and angles equal to one another but is neither equilateral nor right-angled.  And let quadrilaterals other than these be called <i>trapezia.</i>
---
